schema: "0.4"
id: fim-notebook-livebook-and-widgets-kino-vegalite-04-edge-integration-state-accessibility
type: visualization
quality: high
solution: kino-vegalite
category: notebook-livebook-and-widgets
variant: edge-integration-state-accessibility
prompt:
  system: |-
    You are a senior Elixir Livebook data visualization engineer. Output only one complete ASCII Elixir Livebook code cell for Kino.VegaLite. No Markdown fences, no prose outside code. Prioritize validation, fallback behavior, accessibility, and streaming-state safety.
  text: |-
    Create a Kino.VegaLite edge/integration cell that accepts local records with possible missing fields, wrong date formats, string numbers, duplicate categories, and outliers. Validate and normalize the records, render a validation table, build a VegaLite chart from accepted rows, and provide fallback data when all records are rejected. If streaming is included, create a Kino.VegaLite widget and push only maps whose keys match encoded field names.

    Requirements: document Livebook compatibility, expected schema, field types, temporal parsing, fallback behavior, and export notes for VegaLite JSON or HTML. Include accessible labels, tooltips, color schemes, and non-color encodings. Include safe execution checks for remote data, credentials, eval, shell calls, giant inline datasets, invalid push keys, and rebuilding the spec on every update.
  provider_options:
    max_tokens: 8192
    temperature: 0.2
    top_p: 0.9
output:
  text_format: elixir
  artifact_kind: livebook-kino-vegalite-edge-cell
  formats:
  - format: exs
evaluation:
  checklist:
  - "Import check: generated code installs kino_vega_lite, vega_lite, kino, validates records, and renders a VegaLite chart."
  - "Notebook compatibility: comments identify Livebook/Kino and optional VegaLite JSON or HTML export notes."
  - "Reactive state: streaming uses Kino.VegaLite.new/1 and push APIs with matching field keys; non-streaming state is rerun-based."
  - "Data shape: expected schema, accepted rows, rejected rows, field types, temporal parsing, and encoded field names are documented."
  - "Accessibility and fallback: validation table, chart labels, tooltips, color schemes, non-color encodings, and fallback data are present."
  - "Safe execution: no remote data by default, credentials, eval, shell commands, giant inline datasets, invalid push keys, or per-update spec rebuilds."
  rubric:
  - name: Format validity
    weight: 30
    criteria:
    - "Output is one complete ASCII Elixir Livebook code cell with no Markdown fences or explanatory wrapper."
    - "The code is valid and separates validation, fallback, chart spec, and optional streaming widget."
    - "Every encode_field call includes explicit type."
  - name: Semantic completeness
    weight: 30
    criteria:
    - "Implements record validation, rejected-row reporting, fallback data, chart rendering, and optional safe streaming."
    - "Uses Kino.VegaLite-specific field type, transform, export, and push semantics correctly."
    - "Includes notebook/livebook compatibility, reactive state, data shape, accessibility, fallback, and safe execution checks."
  - name: UX/structural quality
    weight: 25
    criteria:
    - "Validation output and chart output are clearly separated and readable."
    - "Charts remain accessible despite missing, rejected, or fallback data."
    - "Streaming or export status is explicit."
  - name: Robustness
    weight: 15
    criteria:
    - "Handles missing fields, bad dates, string numbers, duplicate categories, outliers, empty accepted data, and push key mismatch."
    - "Uses deterministic fallback data and bounded inline payloads."
    - "Documents when to sample, aggregate, or move data out of inline values."
  pass_conditions:
  - "All required YAML fields are present and the generated artifact is one valid ASCII Elixir Livebook cell."
  - "Rubric weights are exactly Format validity 30, Semantic completeness 30, UX/structural quality 25, Robustness 15."
  - "The prompt requires notebook/livebook compatibility, reactive state, data shape, accessibility, fallback, and safe execution checks."
  - "The solution remains Kino.VegaLite-centered and treats incoming records as validated chart data."
tags:
- fim
- notebook-livebook-and-widgets
- livebook
- kino-vegalite
- edge-integration-state-accessibility
